## 2. SHIPPED.oot x86 sentence

  openOODA/SHIPPED.oot:34 (quoted in full):

    - Standalone x86_64: `oodac emit-x86 fixtures/open69_hello.oo`
      writes `_start` that prints Hello; `as`+`ld` runs it. Product
      `oodac/oodac emit-x86 fixtures/hello.oo` folds greet+concat to
      `Hello, openOODA Developer!` (lock: `scripts/x86_hello_smoke.oo`).
      Harvest const ALU/if/let/mix including `< <= >=` as+ld locks:
      `scripts/x86_*_smoke.oo`. Leftover-ident, leftover-plus-print,
      and while/for leftover `ERR` with no `_start`. Two-arg SysV
      `snd` lea `%rdi`/`%rsi` then `call`; identity frame push
      `%rbp` / mov `%rsp`,`%rbp` / pop `%rbp`; `.bss` bump concat
      `yy`+`zz` → `yyzz` (`.skip 4096`, `.Lcpy`); overflow
      2048+2048+1 `ERR` x86 buf no `_start`;
      `println(greet("World"))` is `call greet` and `Hello, World!`.
      Locks: `scripts/x86_snd_smoke.oo`,
      `scripts/x86_frame_smoke.oo`, `scripts/x86_cat_smoke.oo`,
      `scripts/x86_buf_ovf_smoke.oo`, `scripts/x86_while_smoke.oo`,
      `scripts/x86_greet_call_smoke.oo`. hello.oo fold still has no
      `call greet`. Not emit-c. Not a complete x86 backend. AArch64
      is residual. Lock: `scripts/open69_x86_smoke.oo`.

  Honest. The lock names match the on-disk smokes (cross-checked in
  §5). The "hello.oo fold still has no `call greet`" line is
  important: the fold is a string-constant fold, not a SysV call. It
  does not claim a real `call greet`.

