## 5. ROADMAP.oot residual line

  openOODA/ROADMAP.oot:183 (Residual section):

    AArch64 product-ELF dispatch is residual. Side emit-aarch64
    hello/const-if .s + clang assemble is a named lock
    (`scripts/aarch64_*_smoke.oo`). Link and qemu run stay
    residual. Standalone x86_64 `emit-x86` is product (OPEN-69).

  Note the framing: x86_64 `emit-x86` is product (OPEN-69). This is
  the same OPEN-69 the phalanx §0 and the SHIPPED sentence cite. It
  is not a `[ ]` work row; it is a `product` row in the residual
  section. PV2 reads this as honest: x86_64 is product, AArch64 is
  residual.

  ROADMAP.oot:159-163 is the "Extra emit (not this cycle unless an
  owner names it)" block. The x86 row is the second `[ ]` of three.
  It is not marked `[x]`. The "not this cycle" framing holds.

